### ==============================================================================
### ReadMore API — VS Code REST Client / Postman / Insomnia Testing Requests
### ==============================================================================
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@authorId = {{createAuthor1.response.body._id}}
@author2Id = {{createAuthor2.response.body._id}}
@bookId = {{createBook1.response.body._id}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 0. Health Check
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name healthCheck
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Accept: application/json

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Author Endpoints (CRUD)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1.1 Create Author 1 (Chinua Achebe) -> Expect 201 Created
# @name createAuthor1
POST {{baseUrl}}/authors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Chinua Achebe",
  "country": "Nigeria",
  "bio": "Renowned Nigerian novelist, poet, and critic regarded as the father of modern African literature."
}

### 1.2 Create Author 2 (Chimamanda Ngozi Adichie) -> Expect 201 Created
# @name createAuthor2
POST {{baseUrl}}/authors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Chimamanda Ngozi Adichie",
  "country": "Nigeria",
  "bio": "Award-winning author of Purple Hibiscus and Half of a Yellow Sun."
}

### 1.3 Get All Authors -> Expect 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/authors
Accept: application/json

### 1.4 Get Author by Valid ID -> Expect 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/authors/{{authorId}}
Accept: application/json

### 1.5 Get Author by Non-Existent ID -> Expect 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/authors/64b0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0
Accept: application/json

### 1.6 Update Author -> Expect 200 OK
PUT {{baseUrl}}/authors/{{authorId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bio": "Legendary author of Things Fall Apart and Anthills of the Savannah."
}

### 1.7 Get All Books by an Author -> Expect 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/authors/{{authorId}}/books
Accept: application/json

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Book Endpoints (CRUD & Population)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2.1 Create Book 1 for Author 1 -> Expect 201 Created (populated with author details)
# @name createBook1
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Things Fall Apart",
  "genre": "Classic Fiction",
  "price": 25.50,
  "publishedYear": 1958,
  "author": "{{authorId}}"
}

### 2.2 Create Book 2 for Author 1 -> Expect 201 Created
# @name createBook2
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "No Longer at Ease",
  "genre": "Historical Fiction",
  "price": 18.00,
  "publishedYear": 1960,
  "author": "{{authorId}}"
}

### 2.3 Create Book 3 for Author 1 -> Expect 201 Created
# @name createBook3
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Arrow of God",
  "genre": "Classic Fiction",
  "price": 30.00,
  "publishedYear": 1964,
  "author": "{{authorId}}"
}

### 2.4 Get All Books -> Expect 200 OK (full author details populated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books
Accept: application/json

### 2.5 Get Single Book by ID -> Expect 200 OK (full author details populated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}
Accept: application/json

### 2.6 Get Book with Non-Existent ID -> Expect 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/64b0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0
Accept: application/json

### 2.7 Update a Book -> Expect 200 OK
PUT {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 27.99
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Part 4 — Business Rules & Critical Thinking Demonstrations
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 3.1 Business Rule 1: No Orphan Books -> Expect 400 Bad Request
# Attempting to create a book with an author ID that does not exist in the database
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Ghost Book",
  "genre": "Mystery",
  "price": 15.00,
  "publishedYear": 2020,
  "author": "64b0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0"
}

### 3.2 Business Rule 2: No Duplicate Titles per Author (Case-Insensitive) -> Expect 409 Conflict
# Attempting to create another book with title "things fall apart" for the same author
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "things fall apart",
  "genre": "Classic Fiction",
  "price": 20.00,
  "publishedYear": 1958,
  "author": "{{authorId}}"
}

### 3.3 Business Rule 3: Schema Limits - Zero or Negative Price -> Expect 422 Unprocessable Entity
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Free Book",
  "genre": "Fiction",
  "price": 0,
  "publishedYear": 2021,
  "author": "{{authorId}}"
}

### 3.4 Business Rule 3: Schema Limits - Published Year in the Future -> Expect 422 Unprocessable Entity
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Future Journey",
  "genre": "Sci-Fi",
  "price": 19.99,
  "publishedYear": 2099,
  "author": "{{authorId}}"
}

### 3.5 Business Rule 3: Schema Limits - Published Year before 1450 -> Expect 422 Unprocessable Entity
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Ancient Manuscript",
  "genre": "History",
  "price": 45.00,
  "publishedYear": 1200,
  "author": "{{authorId}}"
}

### 3.6 Business Rule 4: Author Delete Policy (Option A - Block Delete) -> Expect 409 Conflict
# Deleting an author who still has associated books is blocked to prevent orphan books
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/authors/{{authorId}}
Accept: application/json

### 3.7 Business Rule 5: Dynamic Search & Filter - By Genre
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?genre=Classic Fiction
Accept: application/json

### 3.8 Business Rule 5: Dynamic Search & Filter - By Price Range (minPrice & maxPrice)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?minPrice=15&maxPrice=29
Accept: application/json

### 3.9 Business Rule 5: Dynamic Search & Filter - Case-Insensitive Search on Title
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?search=arrow
Accept: application/json

### 3.10 Business Rule 5: Combined Filters & Dynamic Sorting (sort=price&order=asc)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?genre=Classic Fiction&minPrice=20&sort=price&order=asc
Accept: application/json

### 3.11 Challenge: Pagination (page=1&limit=2) -> Returns { total, page, limit, totalPages, results }
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?page=1&limit=2
Accept: application/json

### 3.12 Business Rule 6: Author Statistics for Author with Books -> Expect 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/authors/{{authorId}}/stats
Accept: application/json

### 3.13 Business Rule 6: Author Statistics for Author with NO Books -> Expect 200 OK with sensible defaults
GET {{baseUrl}}/authors/{{author2Id}}/stats
Accept: application/json

### 3.14 Delete Author with NO Books (Author 2) -> Expect 200 OK
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/authors/{{author2Id}}
Accept: application/json
